  "solution": "The logic followed here is : \n\n \n• **3rd number × 2 = 2nd number**\n \n• **2nd number × 2 = 1st number**\n\nSo,\n\n \n• Option - (1) : (600 – 300 –150)\n\n​150 × 2 = 300\n\n300 = 300 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n300 × 2 = 600\n\n600 = 600 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (2) : (400 –200 –50)​\n\n​50 × 2 = 200\n\n**100 ≠ 200 (LHS ≠ RHS)**\n\nAnd,\n\n200 × 2 = 400\n\n**400 = 400 (LHS = RHS)**\n\n \n• Option - (3) : (1000 –500 –250)​\n\n​250 × 2 = 500\n\n500 = 500 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n500 × 2 = 1000\n\n1000 = 1000 (LHS = RHS)\n\n \n• Option - (4) : (200–100 –50)\n\n​50 × 2 = 100\n\n100 = 100 (LHS = RHS)\n\nAnd,\n\n100 × 2 = 200\n\n200 = 200 (LHS = RHS)\n\nHence, **\"Option - (2)\"** is the correct answer.\n\n7b:Tf27,\n&",
